=== CORRECTION (kind-pasteur, after reading the data) ===
The concluding lines printed above were WRITTEN INTO THE SCRIPT BEFORE the data was seen
and are REFUTED by it.  Internal arithmetic resonance does NOT explain large q(K):
median smallest-reduced-ratio-sum is 524 in the LOW-q half and 515 in the HIGH-q half --
statistically identical, and the gcds are 1 in both medians.

WHAT THE DATA ACTUALLY SHOWS: q(K) is large exactly when the killer speeds are NEARLY
EQUAL to one another (multiplicatively tight), not when they are arithmetically resonant:
  q = 1.45e-2  K = [257, 258, 263]   (spread 2.3%)   <- largest
  q = 5.82e-3  K = [211, 226, 230]   (spread 9%)
  q = 3.66e-3  K = [176, 182, 224]   (spread 27%)
  q = 6.63e-4  K = [417, 544]        (spread 30%)    <- smallest
MECHANISM: near-equal killers have nearly COINCIDENT bad sets, so the block safe set has
long runs and a large H-oscillation; well-separated killers interleave and equidistribute,
giving small q.  So the (BG-K) obstruction is TIGHT MULTIPLICATIVE CLUSTERING within the
killer block, and the natural route to closing it is that a near-equal pair contributes
essentially ONE constraint (suggesting an effective-LRC(13) argument), NOT a relation
witness.  Recorded as an honest hypothesis-refutation.
